    "_comment": "SMPL-X -> Unitree Go2 (quadruped) as an UPRIGHT biped: human arms -> front legs, human legs -> rear legs, spine -> go2 body held VERTICAL so it walks on its hind legs. base rot_offset [0,0.707107,0.707107,0] tilts the go2 nose up. Same design as bvh_lafan1_to_go2.json; the orientation was derived by composing the horizontal base offset with a 270deg body-pitch. If the nose comes out tilted for SMPL-X data, retune this quaternion. go2_mocap.xml has widened joint limits so the hind knees can straighten into this pose. SCALES CALIBRATED BY SEGMENT LENGTH to root 0.50/arms(front) 0.65/legs(rear) 0.50 (was 0.55/0.55/0.60): here EVERY joint is position-tracked, so the scale must make each scaled human SEGMENT equal the fixed robot segment (Go2 thigh==calf==0.213 m). Human segments ~ thigh 0.44/shin 0.42/upper-arm 0.33/fore-arm 0.25 m => legs 0.213/0.43~=0.50, arms 0.213/0.33~=0.65 (matches the proximal upper-arm; fore-arm ends slightly short because the human arm is unequal while the robot front leg is equal). A prior 0.70/0.79 pass over-scaled the thigh and pushed targets past reach. root 0.50 keeps the stance consistent so the rear feet reach the ground; fine-tune per-segment if elbow/knee tracking drifts.",
